    slug: "claude-ai-guide",
    title: "How to Use Claude AI for Everyday Tasks",
    excerpt: "Claude is an AI assistant from Anthropic — it's known for being thoughtful, nuanced, and particularly good at longer writing and analysis.",
    body: "Claude is an AI assistant built by a company called Anthropic. Like ChatGPT, you can have a conversation with Claude in plain English and it will help you with an enormous range of tasks — drafting emails, explaining confusing documents, summarizing long articles, answering questions, brainstorming ideas, and much more.\n\nClaude has developed a reputation for being particularly careful and nuanced in its responses. Where some AI assistants give a confident answer even when they're uncertain, Claude tends to acknowledge what it doesn't know and flag when a question would be better answered by a professional. It's also very good at handling long documents, like a lease agreement, a medical report, or a lengthy letter, and pulling out the key points you need to pay attention to.\n\nTo get started, go to claude.ai in a web browser on your phone or computer. You can also download the Claude app from the App Store (iPhone) or Google Play (Android). Create a free account using your email or your Google account.\n\nThe free tier gives you a generous number of messages per day with Claude. Claude Pro, at about $20 per month, gives you higher message limits, priority access when the service is busy, and the ability to work with very long documents (up to about 200,000 words at once — roughly the length of a full novel).\n\nTo start a conversation, type your request in the message bar. Some practical uses: paste a confusing letter from your insurance company and ask Claude to explain it in plain English; paste a recipe and ask it to scale the ingredients for a larger group; describe a problem you're having with a device and ask for troubleshooting steps; draft a response to a difficult email you need to write.\n\nOne of Claude's most practical features is document analysis. Click the paperclip or attachment icon and upload a PDF — a bank statement, a medical summary, a contract, a bill — and then ask Claude specific questions about it. For example: \"What is the monthly premium?\" or \"Are there any fees if I cancel?\" or \"What does this medical term mean?\"\n\nProjects let you create separate ongoing conversations for different topics — one for recipes, one for a home renovation project, one for helping with a grandchild's school assignment. Each project keeps its context separate so Claude doesn't mix them up.\n\nPrivacy note: Anthropic uses conversations to improve Claude by default. You can opt out of this in your account settings under Privacy. Conversations are not shared publicly.\n\nClaude is a powerful tool for thinking through problems and handling writing tasks. As with any AI, don't rely on it for medical diagnoses, legal decisions, or financial advice without checking with a qualified professional.",
